{"builder":"Build a new tool, jsonl-lint, as a workspace under packages/jsonl-lint, and open one pull request that meets every acceptance line of https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102. At present packages/ does not exist; the root package.json already lists packages/* as workspaces; .github/workflows/test.yml runs `npm ci` then `npm test` on Node 22.\n\nSteps:\n1. Create packages/jsonl-lint/package.json with name `jsonl-lint`, `\"type\": \"module\"`, `\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }`, a `bin` entry `{ \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" }`, engines node >=22, and no `dependencies` (no devDependencies either; use only node: built-ins).\n2. Create packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js, a plain ES module that exports `lint(text)`. Split text on `\\n` (strip a trailing `\\r` per line so CRLF works). Line numbers are 1-based. Skip lines that are empty or only whitespace. JSON.parse every other line, including a last line with no terminating newline (a torn/unterminated last row must be checked, not dropped). Return an array of `{ line, error }` objects, one per invalid row, in order, where error is the parse error message; return [] when all rows are valid. A trailing newline at the end of the file must not produce an error.\n3. Create packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang (make it executable, git mode 100755). It takes one file argument. With no argument, print a usage message to stderr and exit 2. If the file cannot be read (missing), print an error to stderr and exit 2. Otherwise read it as UTF-8, run lint, print `<file>:<line>: <error>` (the file as given on the command line) to stdout for each invalid row, and exit 1 if there were any, 0 if none.\n4. Write node:test tests in packages/jsonl-lint/test/ (e.g. test/lint.test.js and test/cli.test.js) that `node --test` picks up from the workspace directory. Cover: a clean file (no errors, CLI exit 0); a bad middle row (reports exactly that line number, CLI prints `<file>:<line>: ` and exits 1); a torn last row with no trailing newline (reported); blank lines (skipped, and line numbers of later rows still count them); the exit codes 0, 1 and 2 (no argument, missing file), running the bin with child_process.spawnSync(process.execPath, [binPath, ...]) and temp files from fs.mkdtempSync(os.tmpdir()).\n5. Create packages/jsonl-lint/README.md: what it does, usage `jsonl-lint <file>`, output format, exit codes 0/1/2, and the `lint(text)` API.\n6. Update the root README.md: replace the \"No tools yet\" bullet in \"What is here\" with a bullet listing `packages/jsonl-lint` and a one-line description.\n7. Run `npm install` at the repo root so package-lock.json includes the new workspace (otherwise `npm ci` in CI fails), and commit the updated package-lock.json. Then run `npm ci && npm test` at the root and confirm it passes, and run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` by hand against a clean file, a bad file, a missing file and no argument to see output and exit codes.\n8. Commit everything and open one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body contains the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow on the PR head to finish; if it fails, read the log, fix, push, and repeat until it is green.","verifier":"Check out the pull request's head. Run every check there. Work in a temp dir (mktemp -d) for test fixtures. Give one PASS or FAIL per check, with the evidence (commands and output).\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\".\nRun: create clean.jsonl with `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n`; create bad.jsonl with `{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{bad\\n{\"c\":3}\\n{\"torn\":` (no trailing newline; line 2 blank, line 3 bad, line 5 unterminated). Run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <tmp>/clean.jsonl; echo $?` and the same for bad.jsonl.\nPASS: clean prints no error rows and exits 0; bad prints a line starting `<tmp>/bad.jsonl:3: ` followed by an error text and a line starting `<tmp>/bad.jsonl:5: ` followed by an error text, no row for lines 1, 2 or 4, and exits 1.\nFAIL: any other exit code, a missing row for line 3 or 5, a wrong line number, an error reported for the blank line or a valid row, or rows not in the `<file>:<line>: <error>` form.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\".\nRun: `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <tmp>/nope.jsonl >out 2>err; echo $?` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js >out 2>err; echo $?`, inspecting err each time.\nPASS: both exit 2 and both write non-empty output to stderr.\nFAIL: either exits other than 2, or its stderr is empty.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\".\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import {lint} from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n{bad\\n')), JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n')))\"`.\nPASS: lint is an exported function; the first result is an array containing an object with `line` equal to 2 and an `error` property; the second is an empty array.\nFAIL: import fails, lint is not exported, it returns something other than an array, or items lack `line` or `error`.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\".\nRun: read packages/jsonl-lint/package.json; read the test files under packages/jsonl-lint; run `npm test --workspace jsonl-lint` (or `cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test`).\nPASS: package.json has name `jsonl-lint`, type `module`, scripts.test is `node --test`, and no non-empty `dependencies`; the tests use node:test and include cases for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines, and the exit codes; the workspace tests pass.\nFAIL: any of those fields is wrong or missing, there are runtime dependencies, one of the five named cases has no test, or the tests fail.\n\nCheck 5 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\".\nRun: `test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md && echo ok`; `grep -n jsonl-lint README.md`.\nPASS: the file exists and the root README.md mentions jsonl-lint as a tool.\nFAIL: the file is missing or the root README does not list it.\n\nCheck 6 — expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\".\nRun: `gh pr view <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,state`; `gh pr checks <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test`; at the head run `npm ci && npm test`.\nPASS: the PR is on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test, its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`, the `test` workflow check at the head commit succeeded, and `npm ci && npm test` passes locally.\nFAIL: the body lacks that text, the test check is failing, pending or absent at the head, or npm test fails.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail):\n- Check that package-lock.json was updated to include the workspace; `npm ci` fails otherwise.\n- Check that CRLF input does not produce false errors, that a file ending in a newline gives no error for the empty final line, and that bin/jsonl-lint.js has a shebang and executable mode.\n- Check the error rows go to stdout and that exit 2 cases print nothing to stdout."}